Z||000011||SCCA FIERO||07-06-99||07:25 PM||||When I was 18 I got a ticket(71 in a 40 zone) and my insurance went throught the roof. I was forced to buy a whimpy car,a Sunbird,althought it was much much better in the snow. I then started to sand the car to be painted and messed around with other things. It ended up staying in the garage for 5 years from 1993 to 1998 and never did get a new paint job. Now I am 27 and our(I am married now)insurance is $130 a month for 2 Fieros a Cavalier and a 94 S-10 ZR2. Funny thing the 86 6 cylinder Fiero was 2 dollars cheaper a month than the 88 4 cylinder Fiero. The 86 6 cylinder Fiero will never see the road again except on it's way to Fiero heavan. It gave it's organs to a younger much better Fiero.
